															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/natvoltaic" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2800867); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2800867&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200790" alt="NatVoltaic" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2800867)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/natvoltaic" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2800867); return false;" >NatVoltaic</a></span> <span class="odate time_1549073740 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Feb 2019 02:15</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4138751">
									

<p>Here's a draft I've whipped up in the span of two days. Originally this was going to be a Clichecon article, but I decided against it and ended up scrapping the idea that would qualify it for the contest.</p>
<p>Thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drannoyingdog" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2425082); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2425082&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1549137453" alt="DrAnnoyingDog" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2425082)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drannoyingdog" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2425082); return false;">DrAnnoyingDog</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/uncle-nicolini" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3487700); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3487700&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1549137453" alt="Uncle Nicolini" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3487700)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/uncle-nicolini" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3487700); return false;">Uncle Nicolini</a></span> for crit! Bonus thanks for Nicolini for coming up with the title.</p>
<p>EDIT: Since I forgot to mention this before, this is part of the in-progress Ad Astra Per Aspera canon &#8212; essentially a vast space opera set in a future post-veil loss Foundationverse. No tag exists for it yet, but a list of all articles in it can be found <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-5753812/tag-suggestion-thread-ii:electric-boogaloo#post-4082389">here!</a></p>

